#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""herd-board — the ONE status panel in the right third of the orchestrator tab (docs/herd-flow-v2.md §3).

Usage: herd-board [--anchor <pane>] [<herd-dir> ...]
       herd-board --open [--anchor <pane>]     (open the panel next to the anchor unless it is live)
       herd-board --once [<herd-dir> ...]      (print one frame and exit; size from COLUMNS/LINES)
       herd-board --selftest                   (offline: synthetic events for every lane + the v1 fallback)
       herd-board --help

Herd dirs: those given plus those listed in ~/.cache/herd-board/<anchor>.herds. The state of a slice is its last
event in <herd>/herd.events.jsonl (read through herd_events.py next to this script); everything live is computed.
Lanes, top to bottom, each drawn only when non-empty:
  1. Queue          ! fix_queued (always first), ◌ queued "starts as no. n" + why it waits (slot, base, memory)
  2. Working        ? herdr reports `blocked` (first, yellow), ● working (⧗ tests/build, ↺ fix round),
                    ✓ reported (report written, idle), ⚠ still, ✕ gone,
                    plus the orchestrator's own subagents (◆) and Workflow runs (▸ with their agents)
  3. Ready to merge one row per package: ◇ accepted (+ why the review waits), … review running (round n/3),
                    ✓ rev'd ✓ + the exact merge word (reviewed on current heads), ✓ rev'd waiting for a partner or
                    base, ⟳ stale (PR head or main moved since review_ok), ! findings
  4. Merged today   numbers from `merged` events plus the GitHub search (HERD_BOARD_ORG)
Each slice row ends dim with age and model·effort from its working event (O·hi = Opus/high). ⇄ marks a file
overlap with another live slice (`herd-clash <herd> --json`, on PATH or next to this script; skipped when absent).
Header: time, `you: n`, `slots n/m (k review)` from `herd-limits` (when present), free RAM, free disk, and the
time of the last human input into the anchor session once that is > 30 min ago.
A herd dir with no herd.events.jsonl but a herd.map is a v1 herd: shown the old way with a dim
"v1 herd — herd-recover migrates it" line, so live herds keep working until `herd-recover` migrates them.

The panel height is shared evenly in the Working lane: one worker gets its progress bar, sentence and step feed,
ten get a line each. Lanes 4 and 5 are pinned to the bottom. Nothing is cut silently: overflow says "+N more".
Closes itself after IDLE_CLOSE_MIN with nothing to show. Never sends keys. Repaints every 5 s.

Worker status contract (<slice>.status.json, written by the worker, English or German keys):
  {"sentence"|"satz": "...", "step"|"schritt": 3, "of"|"von": 6, "missing"|"fehlt": "...",
   "short"|"kurz": "3-6 words", "pr": "PR #12" | "api #12 + ui #4" | "https://github.com/o/r/pull/12"}

Environment:
  HERD_BOARD_LANG   en (default) | de
  HERD_BOARD_ORG    GitHub owner(s), comma-separated, for bare repo names and the "merged today" search
                    (unset: no search; gh resolves repos from the slice's worktree)
  HERD_BOARD_REPOS  short names used in refs, e.g. "api=my-api,ui=my-ui,ma=other-owner/agent"
  HERD_BOARD_DISK   path whose free space the header shows (default: the first herd dir, else the cwd)
  NO_COLOR          plain text
"""
import calendar, glob, json, os, re, shlex, shutil, subprocess, sys, textwrap, time, unicodedata

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, HERE)
try:
    import herd_events as he  # the one source of herd state; never forked here
except ImportError:  # board copied without its core: v2 herds show an error line, v1 herds still render
    he = None

CACHE = os.path.expanduser("~/.cache/herd-board")
IDLE_CLOSE_MIN = 5      # nothing to show for this long -> the panel closes itself
AGENT_DONE_KEEP_MIN = 2  # a finished subagent stays visible this long
START_GRACE_S = 180     # a fresh `working` event whose pane herdr does not list yet is "starting", not "gone"
ORGS = [o.strip() for o in os.environ.get("HERD_BOARD_ORG", "").split(",") if o.strip()]
ORG = ORGS[0] if ORGS else ""
REPOS = dict(p.strip().split("=", 1) for p in os.environ.get("HERD_BOARD_REPOS", "").split(",") if "=" in p)
SHORT = {v.split("/")[-1]: k for k, v in REPOS.items()}

LANG = "de" if os.environ.get("HERD_BOARD_LANG", "").lower().startswith("de") else "en"
